# Shipping documents

Shipment documents currently live on shipment records:

`shipments/{id}`

inside:

`documents[]`

Existing document fields include:
- `name`
- `path`
- `contentType`
- `size`
- `uploadedAt`

Example storage path:

`shipments/{shipmentId}/invoice.pdf`

Current document flow:

Load user shipments
→ read `documents[]`
→ create signed URL from Supabase using `path`
→ open PDF or image inside the app

PDF viewing uses:
`pdfrx`

IMPORTANT:

Do not assume that a document `type` field exists unless it is verified in the current code and data model.

If document categories are added later, preserve compatibility with older document entries that do not contain a `type`.

Cargo/shipping manifest documents are NOT the same as:

`android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`

The AndroidManifest.xml file is Android application configuration only.

# Localization

Use the existing localization system.

Existing localization components include:
- `AppLocalizations`
- `LocaleController`
- `lib/l10n/`

Supported languages:
- English `en`
- Arabic `ar`
- French `fr`

Rules:

- Never create a second localization system.
- Reuse and extend the existing localization implementation.
- All new user-facing static text must use localization.
- Do not hardcode user-facing text when localization should be used.
- Arabic must support RTL correctly.
- English and French must remain LTR.
- Changing the language must not hide any information.
- All three languages must expose the same functionality and data.
- Changing locale should not unnecessarily reload Firebase, Firestore, or Supabase data.
- Dynamic backend data must remain unchanged.

Do not translate or modify:
- customer names
- tracking numbers
- shipment IDs
- user IDs
- phone numbers
- emails
- prices
- database IDs
- storage paths
- raw backend values

Translate only the UI labels around those values.

# Status values

Backend status values must remain stable.

For example, if Firestore stores:

`in_transit`

do not change the stored value.

Only translate its display label.

Example:

Backend:
`in_transit`

English:
`In Transit`

Arabic:
`قيد النقل`

French:
`En transit`

Never change backend enum/status values only for localization purposes.

